{
  "a1": "The National Cancer Institute (NCI) focuses on research and training to stay a leader in cancer education. Research is done every day to improve the quality of healthcare. You can read about NCI’s research by looking at the researchers’ profiles. Training graduates is important to keep healthcare quality high and to share knowledge well.\n\nNCI is a training place where graduates see many clinical activities, from educational programs to patient care. Postgraduate trainees in clinical oncology, radiotherapy, surgical oncology, and gynecological oncology train here, leading to degrees awarded by the Post-Graduate Institute of Medical University of Colombo. There are ongoing educational activities for clinicians, postgraduate trainees, nurses, and paramedical staff, such as journal clubs, clinical lectures, and clinical audits. Research and training happen in facilities like the Auditorium, IT Lab, Library Facilities, Hospital Statistics Department, and a designated Research Area (coming soon).",
  "a2": "The National Cancer Institute (NCI) does research and training to stay a leader in cancer education. They do research every day to make healthcare better. You can read about their research by checking the researchers’ profiles. Training graduates helps keep healthcare quality high and share knowledge well.\n\nNCI is a training place where graduates see many clinical activities, like educational programs and patient care. Postgraduate trainees in clinical oncology, radiotherapy, surgical oncology, and gynecological oncology train here, leading to degrees from the Post-Graduate Institute of Medical University of Colombo. They also teach clinicians, postgraduate trainees, nurses, and paramedical staff through journal clubs, clinical lectures, and clinical audits. Research and training happen in the Auditorium, IT Lab, Library Facilities, Hospital Statistics Department, and a Research Area (coming soon).",
  "repair_notes": "removed unsupported generalization about graduates; aligned wording closely with source and kept it simpler without adding facts"
}

